TEXT -8 224 Left 2 !.tran 0 0.31s 0.2s 100us
TEXT -8 232 Left 2 !.param tdv=1 tdt=1 fn1=50 omega_n={2*pi*fn1}
TEXT 16 96 Left 2 ;If only L without C :\nVoltage spike is also dependent of the speed of\nthe switcher\nIf the switcher has longer time to switch or the \nresistance of the switch is not immediately high\nthe energy has time to decrease and so the voltage \nspike is much smaller  \n(Parameter Vt,Vh of the switch for continous \nresistance change)
TEXT 240 80 Left 2 ;Approx -18kJ of energy must be decreased to zero\nALT+Klick on L \nThen zoom to the energypeak and STRG+Klick of the resultant trace -> approx -18kJ\nor load the Plot settings file
TEXT 64 64 Left 2 ;Test also with Switcher with a continous resistance value  (Parameter vt=0.5,vh=-0.4) for much smaller and longer lasting Spike
TEXT 240 144 Left 2 ;Comparison of the energy before (1s) of a power halve wave\nALT+Klick auf L\nZoom and get only one halve wave (x-value changed)\nMeasure x-value with Cursor at Y=0 \nSTRG+Klick at the powertrace -> approx 18kJ\nor load the Plot settings file
TEXT -288 -8 Left 2 ;For comparison of the energy before/after open after simulation the plotfile\nVoltageSpikes_switching_inductances_energy.plt\nPlot Settings/Open Plot Settingfile\nYou can also execute the .meas file energy.meas via FILE/ExecuteMeasScript\n(You have to activate=click the waveform window before)
TEXT -8 240 Left 2 !.options plotwinsize=0 numdgt=10
TEXT -280 120 Left 2 ;The maximal energy is at switching at current max.
TEXT -280 160 Left 2 ;Spikes occur because the energy of the open\ncircuit cannot go immeadeately to zero\nIf the switching time is very short U have to be\nvery high so that U*I*dt = energy is decreased fast \nto a zero value.\nThrough the capacitance the energy can be \ndecrease slower. If C is not present the \nsituation is more severe (Test it with smaller values\nof C). At a real switcher the energy is burned in\nthe electric arc of the switcher and also the switcher\nis constructed to switch at current zero
TEXT 88 312 Left 2 ;; Important small timestep for accuracy (Voltage source used for breakpoints)
TEXT -152 304 Left 2 ;Breakpoints for Halfewave
TEXT -32 304 Left 2 ;Breakpoints for spike
TEXT 232 208 Left 2 !.meas TRAN Energy INTEG V(N002)*Ix(U4:L1_1) FROM 95ms to 100ms ; Halvewave
TEXT 272 216 Left 2 ;right click on .meas line and press TEST
TEXT 232 224 Left 2 !.meas TRAN Energy2 INTEG V(N002)*Ix(U4:L1_1) FROM 100ms TO 100.00011ms ; Spike
